From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 19:30:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: hold 1024 JIT pool images, and keep a full alias table
 loud

The Rockstar Games Launcher's tree had 338 live image copies when Social
Club's second CEF browser started, and each CEF process adds about 50; the
full Social Club tree (a browser, its network and storage services,
renderers and utilities) would pass this table's 512. Every live image is
also pushed to every process's emulator, whose table held 256: the CEF
network and storage services and the second browser refused their late
images, secur32 among them, and died in its delay-load thunk (PLA-373).

The table now holds 1024 images, and FEX's per-emulator alias table the
same (patches/fex 0046); the two must stay in step. A refused alias was
logged 8 times per session; now the first 64 and then one in 256 are,
each with the running count.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-16-alias-table-cap-phone.md
Offered-upstream: no; the JIT pool is Madeira's own iOS code
---
 build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c | 16 ++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
index 6ebdb8f..a23248f 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
@@ -149,7 +149,12 @@ WINE_DECLARE_DEBUG_CHANNEL(virtual_ranges);
  * pseudo-process child's x64/EC set in one table. 64 overflowed at exactly
  * the 65th image (Thumper under desktop, 2026-07-06): concrt140 copied but
  * never registered → raw-VA DllMain call → unfixable exec-fault loop. */
-#define IOS_JIT_MAX_MAPPINGS 512
+/* 1024 (PLA-373): the Rockstar Games Launcher's tree with its Social Club CEF
+ * processes had 338 live images when its second browser started, and each CEF
+ * process adds about 50. Every live image is also pushed to every process's
+ * emulator, so FEX's IosAliasEntries (kMaxEntries, patches/fex 0046) must hold
+ * at least this many: keep the two in step. */
+#define IOS_JIT_MAX_MAPPINGS 1024
 struct ios_jit_mapping {
     void *pe_base;      /* Original PE image base address (unix mapping) */
     void *jit_base;     /* JIT pool RX address */
@@ -3277,13 +3282,16 @@ static ios_alias_cb_t ios_jit_alias_pushback_cb = NULL;   /* non-NULL once any p
 
 /* An emulator refused an alias: its table is full, and every x64->EC call into
  * the image takes the exec-fault redirect instead (ml1106). */
+/* PLA-373: the first 64 refusals, then one in 256, each with the running total,
+ * so a full table stays visible for as long as it refuses. */
 static void ios_alias_note_refused( void *peb, unsigned long long pe, unsigned long long jit,
                                     unsigned long long size )
 {
-    static int said;
-    if (said++ < 8)
+    static unsigned int refused;
+    unsigned int n = __sync_add_and_fetch( &refused, 1 );
+    if (n <= 64 || !(n % 256))
         dprintf( 2, "[jit-alias] PLA-310 emulator of peb=%p FULL: image %#llx+%#llx -> %#llx NOT registered"
-                    " -- its calls will fault-redirect\n", peb, pe, size, jit );
+                    " -- its calls will fault-redirect (refusals so far: %u)\n", peb, pe, size, jit, n );
 }
 
 /* Push one alias to every process's emulator: an image's PE range is unique in
